Z||000000||U Wanna Race||10-15-2001||03:26 AM|||| I have an 85 4 cyl carburated and I was wondering if there is a way to fuel inject it and if so how hard is it.  Also if there is a way to fuel inject it are there turbos for a 4 cyl?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Pontiaddict||10-15-2001||04:07 AM||||     |<BR>\/<P><p>[This message has been edited by Pontiaddict (edited 10-15-2001).]||209.69.222.114||reg||1
Z||000002||Pontiaddict||10-15-2001||04:08 AM||||All Fieros came from the factory with fuel injection. The 4 cyl uses throttle body fuel injection, which kind of looks like a carb, but it is fuel injection. If your car actually has a carburetor on it, then someone changed it from EFI.||||reg||1
Z||000003||U Wanna Race||10-15-2001||11:52 AM||||Ok.  Then what is the difference between TBI and Ported?||||reg||1
Z||000004||terryk||10-15-2001||12:05 PM||||The injectors are in the throttle body rather than the ports.||||reg||1
Z||000005||erikred||10-15-2001||03:59 PM||||No turbo kits are available for the 4 cyl. However, it is not that difficult to turbo charge a 4 cyl. by using mostly parts from a junk yard.||||reg||10
Z||000006||HummelHund||10-15-2001||04:47 PM||||A side note, I saw a multi-port injection intake manifold w/ injectors and ECM for a Jeep 2.5L I-4 on ebay. I have heard this is the same engine as is in our Fieros. Is it, and if so, could Multi-port Injection be retrofitted to a TBI Duke?<BR>TIA<P>------------------<BR>Sean W.<BR>'84 SE, The "Buzz Bomb". (restoration project/daily driver)<BR>'84 SE (Dad's Project)||||reg||1
